  }))), "Future Improvements"), mdx("p", null, "There are several ways the approach could be improved in future work. One limitation of the current model is that it relies mainly on handcrafted feature groups and a single\nclassifier. Performance could be improved by using a pairwise model such as a Siamese network or a transformer fine-tuned directly on text pairs, which would allow the system to\nlearn authorial style differences more end-to-end. Another direction is using data augmentation, such as splitting long spans into multiple segments or paraphrasing sentences to\nimprove robustness."), mdx("p", null, "The model also struggles when one span is very short, so adding minimum-length filtering or specialized short-text embeddings could help. Additional stylometric features such as\nPOS tag patterns, sentence-level rhythm, or syntactic complexity may also provide more author-specific signals. Finally, ensembling multiple models (e.g., XGBoost + a neural model)\ncould help reduce variance and improve overall macro F1 performance on both classes."));
